OrionLayer open fix 70 — the player's language, and its files from another install
==================================================================================

Work order 200 (Part C, German). orion2re on `orionlayer-local`, on top of
f031cbad (open fix 69). src/game only, every line under ORION2RE_EXT.

WHAT IS MISSING. The original reads its language from LANGUAGE.INI at
start (Set_Mox_Language_, mox2.cpp:222-236) and opens each language's own
files by it: GER_HELP.LBX (textbox.cpp:25), HGSTRNGS.LBX (harold.cpp:1531),
estrGERM.lbx (estrings.cpp:18), HERODATG.LBX (harold.cpp:51), GERTECD.LBX
(design.cpp:1025), GERSKLLS.LBX (officer.cpp:3474), GERCRDTS.LBX
(mainmenu.cpp:604), the German font. This build reads the file and throws
the number away: `MOX::_settings.language = 0` (mox2.cpp:235), and again in
Reload_Language_Strings_ (loadsave.cpp:1788). And an install bought in one
language holds that language's files only, so a player with an English and
a German MOO2 has the German files in the other folder.

WHAT THIS ADDS.
  1. ORION2RE_LANGUAGE (0-4, the settings dialog's numbers: 1 German), read
     where the build forced 0 (`MOX2::Ext_Language_`). Unset: 0, as before.
  2. ORION2RE_LANGUAGE_DIR: the last place a READ is looked for when the
     game's folder (and the original's CD path, ORIONCD.INI) cannot serve it
     (vfs_detail::Resolve_Raw_Asset_Path_). Writes never reach it — vfs::fopen
     refuses every mode but read. Unset: nothing changes.
  3. ORION2RE_LANGUAGE_FILES (comma separated, any case): the files the
     language owns, read from ORION2RE_LANGUAGE_DIR FIRST. An English
     install can hold English copies under the German names (Data's
     DIPLOMSG.LBX and EVENTMSG.LBX are DIPLOMSE / EVENTMSE byte for byte), so
     "last" would read the English text; every other file stays the game
     folder's own (its patched HELP.LBX, HESTRNGS.LBX, CMBTSHP.LBX).

OrionLayer's start sets both from the player's settings (core/lang.
engine_env): Deutsch in Game Settings, and the folder named with
tools/language_files.py, and the German files as the owned list.

NOT CHANGED. The settings dialog's own language choice still reloads the
strings (loadsave.cpp:449-456) — into the language the starter asked for,
as it reloaded into 0 before. MOX.SET keeps the language byte the game
writes (byte 210 of its session part); it is set again at every start.

Proof (work order 200): a German engine with an English game folder and
the German files of a Steam 1.31 in the other folder — the turn summary,
the leader offer, the battle panel, the audience ("Womit kann ich dienen"),
the sidebar's "Spielzüge" and "FP" in German, natively.
